      "writtenOn": "2026-02-25T18:57:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had discussed this briefly with Sid before he left his comments.\n\nI think we should also look at the sustainability of this approach and what we are trying to achieve.\n\nSustainability: What happens when \"we\" want to support another vendor module like this one?\n\nMy original thoughts about this were that: 1. We would provide the source (as part of ACK) and that Pixel would of course build it, just like they probably build some other in-tree drivers as vendor modules, and they would suggest  2. We would pick up build failures via the allmodconfig target. 3. We might supply a DDK or some recipe for other partners to use.\n\nThe next step up is to ensure that a communal symbol list is present and maintained. However, this is not really meaningful if partners are supplying cfg and mac as vendor modules!\n\nSo I think we need more clarity around the aims, plan and costs / benefits here.",
      "parentUuid": "218989b8_104b5935",
      "revId": "f2d8540645ba68afafc440508fbd8775dc521b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d4bec3d_bb845586",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
